Purpose: HSTS state and certificate exceptions ignore the container (userContextId) in their keys, so one space's choices apply to every space. Add prefs security.hsts.isolate_by_user_context and security.cert_override.isolate_by_user_context (default false, so Firefox is unchanged); when set the container is part of the key, certificate exceptions no longer fall back to the default container's, and HSTS entries stored before the change are not migrated into other containers. Upstreamable: yes, behind the prefs (the interface comments in nsISiteSecurityService.idl still say HSTS is not isolated; left untouched to avoid an IDL rebuild).
Test: MOZCONFIG=swell/mozconfig ./mach test swell/tests/app/isolation/browser/browser_security.js --headless

diff --git a/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml b/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
index 17f9237d1f05..9117d347320d 100644
--- a/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
+++ b/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
@@ -19325,6 +19325,20 @@
   value: false
   mirror: always
 
+# Keep HSTS state apart per container (userContextId) instead of sharing it
+# between all containers of a profile.
+- name: security.hsts.isolate_by_user_context
+  type: RelaxedAtomicBool
+  value: false
+  mirror: always
+
+# Keep certificate exceptions apart per container and do not fall back to the
+# exceptions of the default container.
+- name: security.cert_override.isolate_by_user_context
+  type: RelaxedAtomicBool
+  value: false
+  mirror: always
+
 # Enable preloaded static key pins by default.
 - name: security.cert_pinning.enforcement_level
   type: RelaxedAtomicUint32
